 "brief": "Our support team handles 12,000 tickets a month with 30 agents. Median first response is 9 hours, and customers who wait more than a day churn at 4% a month against 1.5% for everyone else. We are choosing between hiring 10 more agents at £38k each a year, buying an AI triage tool for £120k a year that the vendor says deflects 35% of tickets, or doing nothing. Our goal is to get monthly churn below 2% within 9 months. Our head of support thinks the tool will deflect only 15% of tickets, not 35%.",
